<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mubarak al-Sabah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1837–1915</span> · Also known as Mubarak the Great</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mubarak al-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabah">Sabah</a>, called Mubarak the Great, was ruler of Kuwait from 1896 to 1915. He took power by killing his half-brothers, and in 1899 signed a secret agreement placing Kuwait under British protection against Ottoman claims. He intervened in central Arabian politics, sheltering the exiled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-saud">Al Saud</a>, and his descendants have ruled Kuwait ever since.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mubarak-al-sabah.jpg" alt="Mubarak al-Sabah" width="320" height="438" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hermann Burchardt (d. 1909) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mubarak_bin_Sabah_as-Sabah.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
